    "path": "knowledge.md",
    "preview": "# Enterprise Data Governance Knowledge Guide for Database: Debit Card Specializing\n\n## 1. Introduction\nThis guide serves as a comprehensive semantic layer for the \"Debit Card Specializing\" database, providing authoritative definitions, metric formulations, and governance standards. It is designed to ensure consistent data interpretation and utilization across enterprise operations.\n\n## 2. Core Entities & Fields\n\n### Customers\n- **CustomerID**: Unique identifier for each customer.\n- **Segment**: Classification of customers into segments such as SME (Small and Medium Enterprises), LAM (Large Account Management), and KAM (Key Account Management).\n- **Currency**: Denotes the currency used by the customer for transactions, primarily 'EUR' (Euro) and 'CZK' (Czech Koruna).\n\n### YearMonth\n- **Date**: Represents the year and month of transactions in 'YYYYMM' format. The first four characters denote the year, and the fifth and sixth characters denote the month.\n- **Consumption**: Total consumption value for the specified period.\n\n### GasStations\n- **Country**: Represents the country where the gas station is located, e.g., 'CZE' for Czech Republic and 'SVK' for Slovakia.\n- **Segment**: Classification of gas stations, including 'Discount' stations.\n\n## 3. Metric Definitions\n\n### Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)\n- **Customer Currency Ratio**: \n  \\[\n  \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{\\text{Count of Customers paying in EUR}}{\\text{Count of Customers paying in CZK}}\n  \\]\n  This metric evaluates the proportion of customers using different currencies.\n\n- **Average Monthly Consumption**:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Average Monthly Consumption} = \\frac{\\text{Total Annual Consumption}}{12}\n  \\]\n  Used to assess monthly consumption trends.\n\n- **Consumption Difference by Currency**:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Difference} = \\text{Total Consumption by CZK Customers} - \\text{Total Consumption by EUR Customers}\n  \\]\n  Measures consumption variance between currency groups.\n\n- **Annual Average Consumption Difference**:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Difference} = \\frac{\\text{Total Consumption in Segment A}}{\\text{Number of Customers in Segment A}} - \\frac{\\text{Total Consumption in Segment B}}{\\text{Number of Customers in Segment B}}\n  \\]\n  Compares average consumption across different customer segments.\n\n- **Percentage Increase in Consumption**:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Percentage Increase} = \\left(\\frac{\\text{Consumption in 2013} - \\text{Consumption in 2012}}{\\text{Consumption in 2012}}\\right) \\times 100\n  \\]\n  Evaluates growth in consumption year-over-year.\n\n## 4. Constraints & Conventions\n\n### Temporal Boundaries\n- **Fiscal Year Format**: Represented as 'YYYYMM', where 'YYYY' is the year and 'MM' is the month. For example, the year 2012 is represented as '201201' to '201212'.\n\n### Currency Formatting\n- **Currency Codes**: Use ISO currency codes such as 'EUR' and 'CZK' for consistency.\n\n### Unit Conversion\n- **Consumption Units**: Ensure all consumption data is standardized in the same unit for accurate calculations.\n\n## 5. Exemplar Use Cases\n\n### Example 1: Customer Currency Ratio\n- **Metric**: Calculate the ratio of customers paying in EUR against those paying in CZK.\n- **Explanation**: This metric helps understand the currency preference among customers, aiding in currency risk management.\n\n### Example 2: Average Monthly Consumption for SME in 2013\n- **Metric**: Determine the average monthly consumption for SME customers in 2013.\n- **Explanation**: Provides insights into monthly consumption patterns, useful for forecasting and resource allocation.\n\n### Example 3: Consumption Difference in 2012\n- **Metric**: Calculate the difference in gas consumption between CZK and EUR-paying customers in 2012.\n- **Explanation**: Highlights consumption behavior differences based on currency, informing pricing strategies.\n\n### Example 4: Annual Average Consumption Difference\n- **Metric**: Compare the annual average consumption between SME and LAM segments.\n- **Explanation**: Assists in identifying consumption trends and segment perfor",
    "truncated": true
  }
}

